    "title": "Two-type-1 fibre spend calibration",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "At the worst strict endpoint a=7m-1 with 4 dividing m, the projective fibres of the minimum-support representation pencil imply that two type-1 slopes force outside spend at least 2m+1 for every type-2 slope. The printed capacity ledger then gives only T<=9m/2, not T<=4m. The same fibre lower bound reaches the calibrated closing spend 9m/4+1 exactly when the two named fibres total at least 25m/4, an additional m/4 beyond the automatic 6m baseline. This is a proved route calibration, not the missing concentration theorem.",
